BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TSHA presents: Jackfruit with special guest Hangaëlle
DTSTART:20260515T220000
DTEND:20260515T220000
UID:650632f43b1630d2c05a4835f353bd9c@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:TSHA Presents: Jackfruit at Standard Time! With support from H
 angaëlle Accolade after accolade\, TSHA has worked her way to the top ech
 elons of UK dance music with scores of multi-country residencies\, in-dema
 nd parties\, and hotly-tipped releases under her belt. Now\, she adds to t
 hose triumphs with the launch of her new record label\, Jackfruit\, after 
 years spent nurturing and evolving her acclaimed event series of the same 
 name. As a DJ\, producer\, multi-instrumentalist and songwriter\, Fareham-
 born artist Teisha has quietly become one of the UK’s most sought-after 
 acts under her TSHA alias. Raised on a musical palette of classic house an
 d garage thanks to her brother’s extensive record collection\, TSHA’s 
 distinguishable sound now arrives at the intersection of melodic house\, B
 alearic\, and high-tempo club music. TSHA’s self-taught dexterity behind
  the decks has earned her shows from Glastonbury to Coachella and beyond\,
  while holding down gigs at some of the UK’s most beloved clubs\, includ
 ing a recent four-week stint at London’s Phonox. With her club night and
  event series Jackfruit\, TSHA puts the audience front and centre with a p
 arty made for “living in the moment”\, with a no-phone policy that cal
 ls for pure connection and euphoria on the dancefloor. To date\, Jackfruit
  has made stops everywhere from Pikes Ibiza to Movement Festival in Detroi
 t. TSHA’s Jackfruit party expands beyond its club form and becomes a rec
 ord label home to ‘Revolution’\, a recent single that muses on “the 
 digital overwhelm” and breaking away from online noise. “‘Revolution
 ’ is a play on Gil Scott-Heron’s ‘The Revolution Will Not Be Televis
 ed’\, but this track is about putting your phone away and living in the 
 moment\,” she says. “As a party\, Jackfruit is a place for escapism. I
 t puts the punter at the centre rather than the DJ\, and allows you to rea
 lly lose yourself.” Hangaëlle is a Toronto-based Mozambican DJ and prod
 ucer. Known for her versatility\, she is especially sought out for her gen
 re-fluid sets that seamlessly weave Afro-electronic music\, club hits\, an
 d global dance sounds into euphoric sonic experiences. Having co-founded K
 uruza and Amaproblem\, and more recently moving into independent curatoria
 l work with the launch of her first solo event\, Mhmmm\, at CODA Nightclub
 \, her contributions to Toronto’s music landscape have continued to esta
 blish her as a key figure in the city’s club culture. See you on May 15t
 h - you don&#x27\;t want to miss this one! ‍
LOCATION:Standard Time\, 165 Geary Avenue #2nd Floor Unit A
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/tsha-presents-jackfruit-with-special-guest
 -hangaelle
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
